:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab2c8761-cb24-5c49-baab-a2303bc03a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448107} :answer-field/id #uuid "74100c42-d4be-5d17-996f-41cc6eef4ed8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449093} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "742b2bf0-8afb-5164-a377-5d2ea7896302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448108} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe1f184-21ca-5a30-a4b4-e7e2d07489d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbe1f184-21ca-5a30-a4b4-e7e2d07489d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448109} :answer-field/id #uuid "5180f33c-1f08-53df-8b94-f11a41c22fc6" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc49fe00-4ce7-5ef1-a571-3c5c05755fd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-1212" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in N∣-1\\le x+1\\le 3}$ and $B={x\\in Z∣{x}^{2}\\le -2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A⊆B$\n- **II.** $A⊈B$\n- **III.** $B⊆A$\n- **IV.** $A⊇B$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $-1\\le x+1\\le 3,$ that is to say, $-2\\le x\\le 2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA={1,2}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality ${x}^{2}\\le -2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB=∅.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false, while $A⊈B$ is true. For example, $0\\in A$ but $0\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true. The empty set is a subset of every set.\n\n- $A⊇B$ is equivalent to $B⊆A,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II, III, and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259616 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54c59e1d-3aed-5da5-920b-29c76019c43a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448116} {:answer/id #uuid "65846218-0157-5d80-8b43-2067671bbc03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54c59e1d-3aed-5da5-920b-29c76019c43a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448116} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fa076dd-8abf-59ea-9d79-6e4ebe730fb3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449098} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "156e6ee8-01e7-5772-b147-fd55c7d3c214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448118} {:answer/id #uuid "51c116a2-fae9-567e-95e7-40ff22cbaba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51c116a2-fae9-567e-95e7-40ff22cbaba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448119} :answer-field/id #uuid "edd5c395-ce4f-5039-81bb-88e680e6bc71" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449099} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d725b57b-1d7c-5344-ba8b-e298e326a6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448120} {:answer/id #uuid "4043b8e8-4044-5bab-95d2-94eb0591fd0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d725b57b-1d7c-5344-ba8b-e298e326a6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448120} :answer-field/id #uuid "27bc06ab-a2f6-5b10-9434-da9802d98339" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449100}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0a1ba57-9eac-5d49-9cdd-f7f25fec8c92" :question/math-academy-id "q-124192" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2v+u+1,\\,y=u-v-2.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $det(A)=-3$\n- **III.** The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2v+u+1 \\\\ u-v-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+2v \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 1=-3.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e39ae7fc-ff0a-5b97-8e13-1f15b12a07e5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Invertible Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34bfe153-da06-5e91-af3f-09f4545070dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448128} {:answer/id #uuid "3edad985-cc26-5a5e-af3e-6700e60c71ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34bfe153-da06-5e91-af3f-09f4545070dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448128} :answer-field/id #uuid "eadb4e27-873a-5521-888f-69f05d97b5e2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ba40652-c044-55c4-8a94-35b541239ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448130} {:answer/id #uuid "947b203f-00c8-5eca-95c1-efce409088a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "947b203f-00c8-5eca-95c1-efce409088a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448131} :answer-field/id #uuid "00944724-9959-5392-a192-85f20e1ec85e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20afd0a3-b0c0-5791-b565-fc7e5b831524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448132} {:answer/id #uuid "9dda385e-2665-5c6a-93bd-f8b119850f77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dda385e-2665-5c6a-93bd-f8b119850f77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448133} :answer-field/id #uuid "36adaa95-128f-5bfd-b7a0-fecb70c1d1da" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3230d0ef-3334-5e9c-bc28-426c4388c6b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-124213" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u-6v-2,\\,y=5v-u+9.\n$$\n\nSuppose that $A$ is the matrix that represents the linear transformation associated with $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $det(A)=4$\n- **III.** The transformation is invertible" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-6v-2 \\\\ 5v-u+9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-6v \\\\ -u+5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|=5\\cdot 2-(-6)\\cdot (-1)=4\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $det(A)\\ne 0,$ the affine transformation is invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259621 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e39ae7fc-ff0a-5b97-8e13-1f15b12a07e5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Invertible Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1daaab98-cbe8-5352-bacb-b5473639f7d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448134} {:answer/id #uuid "61d8fcde-639e-51e8-ad9a-369bc099832e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61d8fcde-639e-51e8-ad9a-369bc099832e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448135} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8bf1e46-3b2c-510e-8fc9-4a0cac9760b0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "441c54c9-8ecc-5a18-9ccb-3f4010752b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448136} {:answer/id #uuid "6a4e6a4b-8eb3-565f-a9a9-d81923448b30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "441c54c9-8ecc-5a18-9ccb-3f4010752b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448136} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cf33e0a-cba5-5662-8a21-99a57c476012" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449108} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb140b7e-c87d-5f72-9d09-3e36fca1601a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448138} {:answer/id #uuid "e8389ee7-d6c3-5f91-8889-ed2eee89b8a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb140b7e-c87d-5f72-9d09-3e36fca1601a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448138} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb21737e-2666-5ebe-87e7-f10521798b5a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67b5699e-cde1-5170-92cc-4d8a2c62f657" :question/math-academy-id "q-124215" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=8u-6v+2,\\,y=4u-3v-1.\n$$\n\nSuppose that $A$ is the matrix that represents the linear transformation associated with $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $det(A)=1$\n- **III.** The transformation is invertible" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8u-6v+2 \\\\ 4u-3v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8u-6v \\\\ 4u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}|=(-3)\\cdot 8-(-6)\\cdot 4=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)=0,$ the affine transformation is *not* invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259623 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e39ae7fc-ff0a-5b97-8e13-1f15b12a07e5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Invertible Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d8644aa-30c8-5f84-95f8-591ae101f520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448140} {:answer/id #uuid "7d56c5c8-75e5-5ea5-96ad-cda45dad43a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d8644aa-30c8-5f84-95f8-591ae101f520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448140} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e36209e-566c-514f-b7e4-aaee36041867" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449110} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea2f9e42-7bf6-5f40-9368-3dda1b852ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448142} {:answer/id #uuid "73d58032-ea3b-55f4-8461-e52c44559040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73d58032-ea3b-55f4-8461-e52c44559040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448143} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e9de89-bea2-5bee-8fc7-7e275041411e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449111} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c502c020-a561-562e-9709-4015d249e451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448144} {:answer/id #uuid "e3628c3d-6abc-5c9d-9e38-4a53a7f3c693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c502c020-a561-562e-9709-4015d249e451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448144} :answer-field/id #uuid "c90de5ac-5ad0-5d21-bc0b-30dee157da82" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8f35619-da30-55db-920a-269c9cc6d2af" :question/math-academy-id "q-124219" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=4u+2v-5,\\,y=2u+v+6.\n$$\n\nSuppose that $A$ is the matrix that represents the linear transformation associated with $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $det(A)=0$\n- **III.** The transformation is invertible" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+2v-5 \\\\ 2u+v+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+2v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 2=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)=0,$ the affine transformation is *not* invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259662 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "346453bf-6ec7-5274-8c95-e05b921f9ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448146} {:answer/id #uuid "c8150770-d90b-59c6-8743-a1aaac54ae0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8150770-d90b-59c6-8743-a1aaac54ae0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448147} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7d34579-5dd5-574b-800f-09b6aea0ce21" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d342b8a4-a9fa-5ec4-a6eb-6a136ee7f657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448148} {:answer/id #uuid "abd09e98-ea9a-5dce-b9eb-228e0b717cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abd09e98-ea9a-5dce-b9eb-228e0b717cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448149} :answer-field/id #uuid "3896a921-2ec9-5c62-ba95-289f7ebf249f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02c44eed-233d-5ab9-b232-1f55f5c23ff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448150} {:answer/id #uuid "f7de793d-0b93-5446-940d-cf97fc0a91ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02c44eed-233d-5ab9-b232-1f55f5c23ff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448150} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cec0683-efdd-5dfb-a194-1aced1608d2e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6b75fa0-1178-5417-bc31-861bbdef5229" :question/math-academy-id "q-124321" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2v-u+2,\\,y=2u+v-5.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $det(A)=-5$\n- **III.** The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2v-u+2 \\\\ 2u+v-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+2v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=(-1)\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2=-5.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1276ca3f-0817-57d0-81fc-4cf3b2b8c257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448152} {:answer/id #uuid "743f6540-a3a1-5ce5-96a0-66ce9f284993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "743f6540-a3a1-5ce5-96a0-66ce9f284993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448153} :answer-field/id #uuid "e00b185e-48ee-59bd-8245-84a19a005d69" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bef7659-decf-5b82-a6f5-3aa7e1134ac2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448154} {:answer/id #uuid "e16c8594-f347-5ced-a1db-0cbf8d2cab8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bef7659-decf-5b82-a6f5-3aa7e1134ac2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448154} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b28f605-aebe-5cbd-9d68-1760caa655fb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c41386b4-b3e8-58e2-8d35-a3b72f57dc4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448156} {:answer/id #uuid "15e896ce-491a-591b-b5ca-d06c641aa278" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c41386b4-b3e8-58e2-8d35-a3b72f57dc4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448156} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bd8e212-89b2-5734-8a82-96a437a9526f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8bc55bfe-e692-5546-9ff3-60dd10f588d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-124322" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u+3v-5,\\,y=2v+u-4.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $det(A)=1$\n- **III.** The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3v-5 \\\\ 2v+u-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3v \\\\ u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3=-1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b403f00-fca0-57ea-8284-891bf3566a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448158} {:answer/id #uuid "843732ab-6614-502e-a8d6-137dd6b219b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b403f00-fca0-57ea-8284-891bf3566a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448158} :answer-field/id #uuid "1800fb93-626f-555b-8257-53399e2b3330" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449119} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d03837d5-08d1-515b-abb3-46fa51e14d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448160} {:answer/id #uuid "5db7ee30-ef80-5d31-b01c-bfcff70810a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5db7ee30-ef80-5d31-b01c-bfcff70810a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448161} :answer-field/id #uuid "fec20ecf-0d1a-5d88-aabc-f6faea141357" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449120} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b74f99e4-3864-593f-90c0-b004a433a43e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448162} {:answer/id #uuid "7a942f96-ec40-5932-89f9-9e68f8f4c5d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a942f96-ec40-5932-89f9-9e68f8f4c5d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448163} :answer-field/id #uuid "398228c4-51eb-52d2-b0e8-75a3a41432b0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449121}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0642bf2f-73a7-542a-b570-be0c81694e35" :question/math-academy-id "q-124324" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=4u-3v-5,\\,y=-2u+2v+4.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $det(A)=2$\n- **III.** The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-3v-5 \\\\ -2u+2v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-3v \\\\ -2u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|=4\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-2)=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $det(A)>0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b72bc2-de18-5a31-bfdf-fdac912549a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448164} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e96f5b-82de-5376-876d-7a84ae9bf74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3e96f5b-82de-5376-876d-7a84ae9bf74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448165} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e27ccb4-b5c0-5a9a-8d03-5e3c15a85d08" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c25dc899-6e5e-5d48-a151-181957ec1b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448166} {:answer/id #uuid "89240879-1b78-5c81-9622-9647e99c0713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89240879-1b78-5c81-9622-9647e99c0713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448167} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5172e33-9775-5938-831d-f44ab65c3dcd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449123} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7080029-1010-516b-b69b-6dabb70fcd57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448168} {:answer/id #uuid "d634558c-1872-5b5c-9aff-88f13ebecb7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7080029-1010-516b-b69b-6dabb70fcd57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448168} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fe4987e-3c97-588e-81f0-536e77edb94f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e2308b7-d41e-52ef-9ac3-a8e7e1231e38" :question/math-academy-id "q-124326" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u-1,\\,y=u-v-2.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $det(A)=-1$\n- **III.** The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-1 \\\\ u-v-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f764cc6-1478-5e54-bd9c-3364a17fabe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448170} {:answer/id #uuid "d7dd388d-1564-519e-9981-ab76abed4493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f764cc6-1478-5e54-bd9c-3364a17fabe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448170} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6b0a775-4d3d-5357-9449-e188e9662c7f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061c1e82-b637-54b1-8c70-6b454f04e2da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448172} {:answer/id #uuid "6421248e-a238-52bf-810c-ffb6d4c763b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6421248e-a238-52bf-810c-ffb6d4c763b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448173} :answer-field/id #uuid "115bb24b-f8bd-5a8f-8b4b-b0b7136582a6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449126} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9714ba44-1e2d-5473-a243-1b09bbe1be18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448174} {:answer/id #uuid "57ff4b59-8350-5857-8238-35585eb2ad54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9714ba44-1e2d-5473-a243-1b09bbe1be18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448174} :answer-field/id #uuid "2da6067f-c334-515f-9b43-3cc92f6a6399" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2083542b-ea7a-58bb-b614-773ec287a63e" :question/math-academy-id "q-124327" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=v-2u,\\,y=u+3v-1.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $det(A)=-7$\n- **III.** The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-2u \\\\ u+3v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2u+v \\\\ u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=(-2)\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1=-7.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "408d4376-fee3-576b-b919-78a362304433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448176} {:answer/id #uuid "8fd32334-9fe7-58f0-b69d-c5e4b56cf483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "408d4376-fee3-576b-b919-78a362304433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448176} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ddf5a2c-e1ba-5ab8-a326-ef2effad6657" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "267cd5a9-bfac-5eed-8904-017678ad4a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448178} {:answer/id #uuid "53ccc33d-0646-52ce-a1eb-2f220bd004a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "267cd5a9-bfac-5eed-8904-017678ad4a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448178} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfeb4901-6e2a-51fc-97ac-18cfb802789c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449129} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ce0c3e5-0bb1-5908-8e46-fb31e5b247a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448180} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d541bc-f6ed-52ec-bf3f-39047b585869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9d541bc-f6ed-52ec-bf3f-39047b585869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448181} :answer-field/id #uuid "de788145-c4bf-5fa3-888f-761cc5fd7fae" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "76a65107-91d8-5259-9f73-6e2fee8f6ae9" :question/math-academy-id "q-124330" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=-2v+1,\\,y=4u-v-5.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $det(A)=-4$\n- **III.** The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2v+1 \\\\ 4u-v-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2v \\\\ 4u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=0\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-2)=8.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $det(A)>0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567" :knowledge-point/title "Circulation in Conservative Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5d80f62-7611-5589-bb35-f2bd8dd2ac54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448188} {: