3} :answer-field/id #uuid "94fc3bec-7574-5b7d-9315-47b094cd5a5b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7b7ddac2-e3bd-590b-a396-56e8108da7f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-125647" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $∇f$ is conservative\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- **III.** ${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567" :knowledge-point/title "Circulation in Conservative Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc049f21-a499-5e1c-bdab-1491bf8bd7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448194} {:answer/id #uuid "70dba20a-9283-5a64-92e1-e818bbe45555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc049f21-a499-5e1c-bdab-1491bf8bd7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448194} :answer-field/id #uuid "74956c98-32c5-5a81-9fd6-d30967d81c85" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449137} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7320a730-56b8-5dc9-935e-a931fcfdca97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448196} {:answer/id #uuid "14225c91-d53e-564c-a75b-2ff3a307db5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7320a730-56b8-5dc9-935e-a931fcfdca97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448196} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4650f15-3ab9-5cbb-8a44-4f88d6ffeef2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "080320d7-6a08-5185-be7b-bf365f7873d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448198} {:answer/id #uuid "556f08e3-7136-594b-bdbf-c1887d7ea54c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "556f08e3-7136-594b-bdbf-c1887d7ea54c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448199} :answer-field/id #uuid "aff3da6e-b916-5bbe-aee8-f8bb72ec84cd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "78e40fa2-e07f-5983-b8b1-ed694102f21b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125648" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)={e}^{y}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $∇f$ is **not** conservative\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise linear path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- **III.** ${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any circle $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Are Independent of Path"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18f626fd-2f98-540d-b753-edd9dc174baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448212} {:answer/id #uuid "78e59729-2e4b-504b-ba62-41d462cf8ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78e59729-2e4b-504b-ba62-41d462cf8ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448213} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb686abc-beb6-5d11-86ca-7abdbef18ce5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449146} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71683e7c-6322-5a71-ac90-c19b267a6348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448214} {:answer/id #uuid "f00e6185-a73b-52ef-a41b-d1ed69644032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71683e7c-6322-5a71-ac90-c19b267a6348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448214} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4f558bf-ebd2-557b-87cd-b12c76af718a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449147} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4525889a-55b7-5233-90f9-f32156fe811b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448216} {:answer/id #uuid "bd070a21-a13b-5f48-b881-ba9cd24e8e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd070a21-a13b-5f48-b881-ba9cd24e8e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448217} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eee062f-dc2e-585b-aa83-7624e11d3b88" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "769cb3f6-44e5-5633-bebf-2f89e5fbe161" :question/math-academy-id "q-125723" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y⟩$ and the points $O(0,0)$ and $A(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F$ is conservative.\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=1,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{OA},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4},$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\sqrt{x},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives exist and are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $F$ is conservative, there exists a function $f$ such that $∇f=F.$ Reconstructing the function $f$ from its gradient in the usual way, we get\n\n$$\nf=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =f(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2})-f(0,0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $F$ is conservative and ${C}_{2}$ has the same initial and terminal points as ${C}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Are Independent of Path"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc29811d-c37a-50df-aab4-72f93f8520df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448218} {:answer/id #uuid "8762f157-eaa2-597a-9b1d-243605b3808f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8762f157-eaa2-597a-9b1d-243605b3808f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448219} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b6e35dc-687e-57d2-8e8c-8130f1de0609" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "216c1876-088b-541b-bc8b-3b55c9ff28ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448220} {:answer/id #uuid "8011e624-2484-5b38-9b4d-6861b9854e15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8011e624-2484-5b38-9b4d-6861b9854e15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448221} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3df687e-6b72-5f94-9d87-c3dd151a791a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a69af186-96bc-5342-b8ef-4f56e480d997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448222} {:answer/id #uuid "0bd53bb0-0f24-5305-b990-ee10ae1a3d7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bd53bb0-0f24-5305-b990-ee10ae1a3d7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448223} :answer-field/id #uuid "77e4d753-8f46-5591-adeb-e05bc4133b31" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "230c0014-f97a-5ec3-b394-cdb780e495b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-125738" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨2x{y}^{2},\\,2y{x}^{2}⟩$ and the points $A(1,1)$ and $B(2,8)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F$ is conservative.\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=255,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=255,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y={x}^{3},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4xy.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives exist and are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $F$ is conservative, there exists a function $f$ such that $∇f=F.$ Reconstructing the function $f$ from its gradient in the usual way, we get\n\n$$\nf={x}^{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =f(2,8)-f(1,1) \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot {8}^{2}-{1}^{2}\\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 64-1 \\\\  & =255.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $F$ is conservative and ${C}_{2}$ has the same initial and terminal points as ${C}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=255.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259861 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Are Independent of Path"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c2c453b-fdb8-55cf-afb7-1e908849cbfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448224} {:answer/id #uuid "ae479600-ccc1-5572-b350-19d3354ed4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae479600-ccc1-5572-b350-19d3354ed4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448225} :answer-field/id #uuid "6da80a74-a157-519f-8264-e73a6be4a502" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449152} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87b93c59-2861-5c27-97be-936d2d58613c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448226} {:answer/id #uuid "72e1316f-268d-5f09-9717-2db567645bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72e1316f-268d-5f09-9717-2db567645bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448227} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e8f95a7-4ae1-5ce1-a2b8-93596df2c4fb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449153} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0ee1943-12e7-5a8e-81ba-c5c9f3220681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448228} {:answer/id #uuid "e385618f-2b72-5771-a5f9-a5240fbcf759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0ee1943-12e7-5a8e-81ba-c5c9f3220681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448228} :answer-field/id #uuid "980f54b2-460e-59b5-8818-a3f1c522f319" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449154} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce4cbbd6-8c6a-5f19-82b0-fb814880d5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448230} {:answer/id #uuid "a7fe2f8d-3d94-55f1-943e-f623b35fa6a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce4cbbd6-8c6a-5f19-82b0-fb814880d5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448230} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a18d9fc-a32b-5b63-b411-bd741ac1d6fe" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7a9fbb00-26f5-5603-96a1-9b8b6773d49d" :question/math-academy-id "q-125789" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨{x}^{2}+{y}^{2},\\,1⟩$ and the points $A(1,0)$ and $B(0,1)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ traversed from $A$ to $B$ in counterclockwise direction.\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{1}{3},$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path.\n- **IV.** $F$ is conservative." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Parameterizing the circle, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{1}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}⟨{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}⟨1,\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Parameterizing the line segment, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{2}(t)=⟨1-t,\\,t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨(1-t)^{2}+{t}^{2},\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,1⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨2{t}^{2}-2t+1,\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,1⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2t-2{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[{t}^{2}-\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{3}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ have the same initial and terminal points, yet\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$\n\nwe conclude that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is path-dependent.\n\n- Statement IV is false. If a vector field is conservative then it is path-independent. Since $F$ is path-dependent, it is not conservative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Are Independent of Path"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fc24743-a02f-5bf0-9839-ac80348908a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448232} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e9b1d4-bf42-5627-ad17-aca33e0e39b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fc24743-a02f-5bf0-9839-ac80348908a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448232} :answer-field/id #uuid "584fe0e6-b857-54a2-9215-9de39aae4c49" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc0dcb42-65e9-55a9-904d-f11371368f91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448234} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd98ec7-8666-52b5-b988-4cbc4f87a080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dd98ec7-8666-52b5-b988-4cbc4f87a080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448235} :answer-field/id #uuid "2031bd8d-6dd0-50f1-a070-e8d5e67ed206" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449157} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd954a98-2cf9-5746-8938-2c98f9e007e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448236} {:answer/id #uuid "5c3d7e0e-e48d-5344-a89f-52e9913c3871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd954a98-2cf9-5746-8938-2c98f9e007e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448236} :answer-field/id #uuid "27965924-fed2-57f3-875b-59e349ddc1fc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449158} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84969817-3dcd-5fdb-8d9f-412b153421cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448238} {:answer/id #uuid "16347b9d-3533-5b71-8f9e-64d4326612b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84969817-3dcd-5fdb-8d9f-412b153421cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448238} :answer-field/id #uuid "065de688-3909-5264-8ef5-ac4a05f8d35e" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8fb181d0-594b-53e9-a69e-a9a120629b9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-125791" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨y,\\,{x}^{2}⟩$ and the points $O(0,0)$ and $A(1,1)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the curve $y={x}^{3},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{5}{6},$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{OA},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path.\n- **IV.** $F$ is conservative." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Parameterizing the curve, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{1}(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨{t}^{3},\\,{t}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{3}+3{t}^{4}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{3{t}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{5}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Parameterizing the line segment, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{2}(t)=⟨t,\\,t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,1⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}t+{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ have the same initial and terminal points, yet\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$\n\nwe conclude that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is path-dependent.\n\n- Statement IV is false. If a vector field is conservative then it is path-independent. Since $F$ is path-dependent, it is not conservative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Are Independent of Path"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6341e8be-459b-5b87-936b-1dfe23420804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448240} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3748af-eec3-5d38-b136-c6716c918337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6341e8be-459b-5b87-936b-1dfe23420804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448240} :answer-field/id #uuid "9201a5f2-4cf8-5f69-a141-20ed8f68831c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449160} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d894e19b-da48-587a-8286-f5de79b1260f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448242} {:answer/id #uuid "c44d9fc1-5023-5b92-bc78-6410e5c51c56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c44d9fc1-5023-5b92-bc78-6410e5c51c56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448243} :answer-field/id #uuid "faa0a59f-3168-5a4c-88fd-9425997ad0d1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449161} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61e55a1e-ab9d-569a-96fc-f107b33b92d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448244} {:answer/id #uuid "0dddf6eb-6699-5d37-8672-fadcf8148fcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61e55a1e-ab9d-569a-96fc-f107b33b92d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448244} :answer-field/id #uuid "36cb0ecc-4dd2-5c8b-8667-c8f0701fba2d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449162} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a4a1778-edf5-5213-be03-411dc4e3fabf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448246} {:answer/id #uuid "1660cf69-a660-5241-9712-d3ea386c916f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a4a1778-edf5-5213-be03-411dc4e3fabf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448246} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc39a85a-6de3-550f-a6b3-e9e0188c695d" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "da972c83-042d-5f07-b576-d951f35ad923" :question/math-academy-id "q-125793" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨{y}^{2},\\,-x⟩$ and the points $O(0,0)$ and $A(4,2)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{5}{6},$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{OA},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{16}{3},$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\sqrt{x},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path.\n- **IV.** $F$ is conservative." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Parameterizing the line segment, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{1}(t)=⟨4t,\\,2t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨4{t}^{2},\\,-4t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,\\,2⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}16{t}^{2}-8t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{t}^{2}-t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{[\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =8[\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Parameterizing the curve, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{2}(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,2].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨{t}^{2},\\,-{t}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨2t,\\,1⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3})-0 \\\\  & =8-\\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ have the same initial and terminal points, yet\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$\n\nwe conclude that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is path-dependent.\n\n- Statement IV is false. If a vector field is conservative then it is path-independent. Since $F$ is path-dependent, it is not conservative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262585 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f6dace5-df44-51df-b091-e335e6a5f910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448248} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c8cb0a-553c-5b2b-9c44-e2a274e9c8da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0c8cb0a-553c-5b2b-9c44-e2a274e9c8da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448249} :answer-field/id #uuid "06b3e70b-d4b0-5c6b-9a9a-45863aa3af04" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449164} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "687570f5-7183-5d5d-8b19-806f9044185e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448250} {:answer/id #uuid "a67a1de3-c4c1-5491-b747-31fbcf7ca0fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a67a1de3-c4c1-5491-b747-31fbcf7ca0fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448251} :answer-field/id #uuid "a14d38ae-80c0-501a-b3f2-640627b28c58" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449165} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "415e1f35-fc43-5b6e-901e-7070d269854c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448252} {:answer/id #uuid "4e293ed4-c95a-522b-ae5b-bf06b8dbb221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "415e1f35-fc43-5b6e-901e-7070d269854c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448252} :answer-field/id #uuid "395f1879-fcec-5312-b747-db939c183eec" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46648507-d053-5fe5-a8fd-c1de8f3e7a6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-1261" :question/problem "For the sets $X={x,y,z},$ $Y={v,w},$ and $Z=X\\times Y,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(x,v)\\in Z$\n- **II.** $(y,w)\\in Z$\n- **III.** $(w,z)\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $X\\times Y$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Y.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $X\\times Y$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/31/316a12102e4be81291f06403815cfb63749b1fd3f463c465294e031543123484.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(x,v),(x,w),(y,v),(y,w),(z,v),(z,w)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d49a7b78-bea1-54e5-8232-3fea0d4eb5a3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Concerning a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad0b2008-bd90-5168-be5c-10de1a5ffdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448260} {:answer/id #uuid "cbfbf81b-2df5-5692-8bdf-b3c476b091e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad0b2008-bd90-5168-be5c-10de1a5ffdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448260} :answer-field/id #uuid "93520d72-452c-50c9-97c6-82b2dfb2f65b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91907250-1b71-5208-9c48-56b624cb208a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448262} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb582a7-2819-5150-ac4e-acd82016b49f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5eb582a7-2819-5150-ac4e-acd82016b49f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448263} :answer-field/id #uuid "665b8c3b-23dd-500c-a6e4-59240a3ea0f9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449171} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32d22f54-d568-5c48-a820-4240015e79dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448264} {:answer/id #uuid "07c32ebf-0bc4-563a-88ae-ed188defb588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32d22f54-d568-5c48-a820-4240015e79dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448264} :answer-field/id #uuid "c13fe396-2f57-59c0-b60c-e1db65afd4f0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "012090a8-b5e2-5e56-87ba-9a6b486504ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-127918" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-11 \\\\ y+7x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The coefficient matrix is not invertible\n- **II.** The determinant of the coefficient matrix is not zero\n- **III.** The lines $x+2y=-11$ and $y+7x=4$ intersect at infinitely many  points" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is true. According to the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem, the determinant cannot be $0.$\n\n- Statement III is false by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262851 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d49a7b78-bea1-54e5-8232-3fea0d4eb5a3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Concerning a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31393764-2a3b-5f94-a8ad-ec6c335171fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448266} {:answer/id #uuid "553375c2-cf85-5f9d-bbb0-2230855cf965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "553375c2-cf85-5f9d-bbb0-2230855cf965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448267} :answer-field/id #uuid "19c7722a-6979-5033-a8fd-f7b21ac292e9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449173} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a40d55b1-98b2-5ff7-b0b5-62a7b770b2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448268} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ed1980-c042-5487-b529-f6a360735551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5ed1980-c042-5487-b529-f6a360735551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448269} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d1d04d4-58b5-55a1-ac37-5e45b973022f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449174} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61b43c99-11a6-57ed-8a16-f4ef4192ec6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448270} {:answer/id #uuid "71013a10-6913-520b-800b-767fdc89601a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61b43c99-11a6-57ed-8a16-f4ef4192ec6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448270} :answer-field/id #uuid "8901af95-d0b6-584c-8098-fd5186cd5e05" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd31265e-20ac-5d02-8e25-ee3bd3fdfd6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127919" :question/problem "Consider a system of two linear equations in two variables, represented by the matrix equation $Ax=b$ in the usual way. Given that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(A)\\ne 0$\n\n- **II.** $A$ is  invertible\n\n- **III.** $Ax=0$ has a nonzero solution" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n1\\. $A$ is invertible.\n\n2\\. The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n3\\. The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n4\\. The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n5\\. $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is true by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d49a7b78-bea1-54e5-8232-3fea0d4eb5a3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Concerning a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193a9a31-72cc-52c6-a705-a7cc0d131106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448272} {:answer/id #uuid "2e608d1e-afec-550f-8c0a-a1b47085d8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "193a9a31-72cc-52c6-a705-a7cc0d131106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448272} :answer-field/id #uuid "84301b7c-4bac-571e-acbc-02ec8c83029b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449176} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75573dd0-ebb2-5a2b-8aa4-6ff78a5f0d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448274} {:answer/id #uuid "a7593381-daab-5f1a-a7a3-7c82d8e103ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75573dd0-ebb2-5a2b-8aa4-6ff78a5f0d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448274} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3bdd369-88e5-5770-a50b-15c5ebdb3612" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449177} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54c547b3-1b9f-57e3-be16-35c6dc9d2854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448276} {:answer/id #uuid "ea577f79-65e8-595e-a0ef-8870c1c707ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea577f79-65e8-595e-a0ef-8870c1c707ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448277} :answer-field/id #uuid "862bba97-dd62-5306-8468-8af85b572b72" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "112c3205-5323-5719-a0c7-431fff65b0ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-127920" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y=-1 \\\\ 3y-x=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The lines $2x-2y=-1$ and $3y-x=1$ intersect at infinitely many  points\n- **II.** The coefficient matrix is not  invertible\n- **III.** The determinant of the coefficient matrix is not equal to zero" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is false by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is true by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69107280-70c4-5ca4-8b64-1e64450165b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448278} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3f6955-4016-59d3-9db9-3955354a9810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a3f6955-4016-59d3-9db9-3955354a9810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448279} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ee137d6-1832-58d0-85d5-575e29a0fa26" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449179} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29bde20c-189c-54ef-b19c-9e8950c65826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448280} {:answer/id #uuid "5a9158da-7221-5175-b881-fdd36f8f42ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29bde20c-189c-54ef-b19c-9e8950c65826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448280} :answer-field/id #uuid "de466e8f-4f63-50c6-b72f-38c520f95211" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6c45389-9701-5934-b1ac-2f11edac2800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448282} {:answer/id #uuid "f20f2e0e-7487-58ee-9feb-810b44ca227a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f20f2e0e-7487-58ee-9feb-810b44ca227a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448283} :answer-field/id #uuid "db9964be-6910-5d74-bd0f-7b3cfcffc16d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "364a18ef-2de8-57d7-9e2f-631eb4651446" :question/math-academy-id "q-127931" :question/problem "Let $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & k\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ where $k$ is a constant such that $k\\ne -3.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(A)\\ne 0$\n- **II.** $Ax=0$ has no solutions\n- **III.** The lines $x+3y=-1$ and $-x+ky=1$  intersect at exactly one point." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & k\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot k-(-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $k+3\\ne 0$ if $k\\ne -3.$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the unique solution to  $Ax=0$ is the trivial one (zero).\n\n- Statement III is true by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nFinally, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba1c76d6-26c8-504d-9404-70d3044b6d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448284} {:answer/id #uuid "52a42a90-a2f2-53a1-a38b-f3fbd471febf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52a42a90-a2f2-53a1-a38b-f3fbd471febf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448285} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1f5a7d6-794e-5b2e-8232-2ef8047378b7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a25b72a-8f61-5c4f-851c-aafa09b763a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448286} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf17fa0-ce5e-57ed-be01-382386d4d6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecf17fa0-ce5e-57ed-be01-382386d4d6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448287} :answer-field/id #uuid "94fe4db0-076c-5d37-abdd-95681679518e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2f82e7b-d0c9-554d-b199-c9cd2d9d3e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448288} {:answer/id #uuid "d21d1cbd-a4f9-59d3-90e9-eebe3afbe948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2f82e7b-d0c9-554d-b199-c9cd2d9d3e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448288} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4af399e-f753-5679-8b6d-af7bd231a29f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "98a38053-dfdc-5995-9d99-1db68e6c6765" :question/math-academy-id "q-127943" :question/problem "Let \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(A)\\ne 0$\n- **II.** $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b$\n- **III.** ${A}^{-1}$ does **not** exist" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is true by the second part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the first part of the invertible matrix theorem, the inverse ${A}^{-1}$ must exist.\n\nFinally, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262876 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4abfb096-6bba-5ea2-bf9c-18957c7e68e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448290} {:answer/id #uuid "5230d7f7-5e35-5729-b0e1-3278e7fe5616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4abfb096-6bba-5ea2-bf9c-18957c7e68e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448290} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ce3286e-5eb6-554c-b5ea-aa0eacd505cd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449185} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e17fb2f-c144-5859-ab19-13769207d987" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448292} {:answer/id #uuid "864b613f-cd1f-51bc-a958-900baa735a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "864b613f-cd1f-51bc-a958-900baa735a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448293} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5f91f5f-9b80-5001-94e4-1a6906434452" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7510f705-ade9-5b16-a00a-8c553aa48c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448294} {:answer/id #uuid "484b7edd-b950-5cae-bafa-4ec7c3c6e9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "484b7edd-b950-5cae-bafa-4ec7c3c6e9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448295} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fafc811-ec3d-58ec-be64-95611287b86a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d4f36ed6-3fc6-5f37-801d-3dafa17482c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-128124" :question/problem "Let \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(A)=0$\n- **II.** $A$ is invertible\n- **III.** $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is true by the second part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nFinally, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262877 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d364ced3-f0b4-5db0-a418-8e753ca019ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448296} {:answer/id #uuid "c073cf48-e7ec-54b8-aa41-5f5dd4380be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d364ced3-f0b4-5db0-a418-8e753ca019ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448296} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fe6ac89-7503-556b-afe3-bc96c1615f30" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e79c11e7-6e9c-5e41-a093-0a00d224cc41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448298} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4b969f-164a-59d2-bd0e-77808fa91ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f4b969f-164a-59d2-bd0e-77808fa91ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448299} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fb139ea-e0aa-5492-9328-5084dd32f1a0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "151b861f-225f-5d93-94c6-8c117995a350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448300} {:answer/id #uuid "503ffa37-1521-58e6-8ba5-365468b412c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "151b861f-225f-5d93-94c6-8c117995a350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448300} :answer-field/id #uuid "262c7598-2a14-5bdc-94d3-bf80698480e8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7887fe01-425a-54fe-9f35-ac58c1eba82c" :question/math-academy-id "q-128136" :question/problem "Let $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 \\\\ -2 & k\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ where $k$ is a constant such that $k\\ne -4.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(A)=0$\n- **II.** The system  $Ax=0$ has exactly one solution\n- **III.** The lines $7x+14y=2$ and $-2x+ky=-3$ intersect at infinitely many points" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 \\\\ -2 & k\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =7\\cdot k-(-2)\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =7k+28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $7k+28\\ne 0$ if $k\\ne -4.$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the unique solution to $Ax=0$ is the trivial one (zero).\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem, the lines must intersect at exactly one point.\n\nFinally, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92ef990e-1cea-5691-add8-a9a4bd107064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448302} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc67608-1f2c-5d22-b921-920a8e4c97a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92ef990e-1cea-5691-add8-a9a4bd107064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448302} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc96e470-5f69-574c-9b9e-c620bf3eb7d7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449191} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63ddb0bf-c7e0-5bed-a309-72dc6fd5a94b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448304} {:answer/id #uuid "7f593a64-253b-5b53-be4d-93a7fd10d52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f593a64-253b-5b53-be4d-93a7fd10d52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448305} :answer-field/id #uuid "df16a0f8-d309-5196-8986-cbcb30f5ac79" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f26b8f8-7a28-5ba9-a92e-f0f01da7dab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448306} {:answer/id #uuid "79cbbda2-7409-51ac-b909-8eaa54f9322b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79cbbda2-7409-51ac-b909-8eaa54f9322b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448307} :answer-field/id #uuid "c942c571-9ddc-5568-9ee7-d107cf23c370" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02aab097-5368-5094-843f-c0ac47beef5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-129058" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+{y}^{2}}{x}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=-1$ gives a line\n\n- **II.** $c=0$ gives a parabola, excluding the origin\n\n- **III.** $c=1$ gives the $x$-axis, excluding the origin" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+{y}^{2}}{x} & =c \\\\ x+{y}^{2} & =cx \\\\ x(1-c)+{y}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1,$ the level curve is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2},$ which is a parabola that opens to the left (excluding the origin). So, I is false.\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curves is $x=-{y}^{2},$ which is a parabola that opens to the left (excluding the origin). So, II is true.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is $y=0,$ which is the $x$-axis (excluding the origin). So, III is true.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c15a454d-c0ca-506d-b884-f5178778ed63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448308} {:answer/id #uuid "c32fe568-db32-54b6-8558-ab5cfc063bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c15a454d-c0ca-506d-b884-f5178778ed63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448308} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ce8677-ff71-54c3-ad56-f3412cdf488f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa79405f-ffc1-5234-ad9c-42a8996c0c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448310} {:answer/id #uuid "d901ccba-6ca6-5ba5-b447-d349fd2445c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa79405f-ffc1-5234-ad9c-42a8996c0c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448310} :answer-field/id #uuid "70ebaa1d-8cd6-5098-9a25-c5f76b89deb4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449195} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5095e664-dc44-568b-aa90-8adbb890de3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448312} {:answer/id #uuid "010f4da8-c1ee-5554-b6b8-f8cf5ae4e818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "010f4da8-c1ee-5554-b6b8-f8cf5ae4e818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448313} :answer-field/id #uuid "93e97ed1-eab4-543d-87b4-43be11f05919" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42b1c0f3-5dd1-53b2-92c2-3218b1cbc331" :question/math-academy-id "q-129063" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=-1$ gives a hyperbola\n- **II.** $c=0$ gives the $y$-axis, excluding the origin\n- **III.** $c=1$ gives the line $y=x,$ excluding the origin" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x} & =c \\\\ y & =cx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1,$ the level curve is the line $y=-x,$ excluding the origin. So, I is false.\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curve is the line $y=0,$ which is the $x$-axis (excluding the origin). So, II is false.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is the line $y=x,$ excluding the origin. So, III is true.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c4244bc-8ceb-5e33-8598-38ab925f8b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448314} {:answer/id #uuid "a4baa4cb-1e55-5d20-9fad-2d8fefbf1372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c4244bc-8ceb-5e33-8598-38ab925f8b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448314} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8142b6d-b401-52da-b7e4-0f8f6f82bcce" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449197} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65643d53-a883-5f0e-b168-41516f263752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448316} {:answer/id #uuid "fe198cb5-4419-5f30-8103-df3f434b8f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65643d53-a883-5f0e-b168-41516f263752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448316} :answer-field/id #uuid "90ca466e-5705-5201-b9a5-5dca1c9735d0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a09c6d3-9e07-5bfa-a9af-913b460366de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448318} {:answer/id #uuid "401bbb80-3136-505b-91b2-a79e6cdcbae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "401bbb80-3136-505b-91b2-a79e6cdcbae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448319} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8a49394-7282-584c-b4ee-30af011d8280" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d967e86-9fda-51c5-b084-5eaf2a90df28" :question/math-academy-id "q-129239" :question/problem "Given the two planes $2x-5y+z+1=0$ and $3x-z+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- **II.** The planes are parallel.\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $2x-5y+z+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-5,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x-z+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,0,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨2,-5,1⟩\\times ⟨3,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =5i+5j+15k \\\\  & =⟨5,5,15⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff5f8263-677b-5643-9c09-fbb882cb5e5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448320} {:answer/id #uuid "7e00f930-9bc2-5a8f-b341-6b3bfb849414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e00f930-9bc2-5a8f-b341-6b3bfb849414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448321} :answer-field/id #uuid "c870b39a-efa3-5b75-abf3-729e6c1bb66c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449200} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddbba897-a72e-574e-bb64-100d9be232c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448322} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6d0ded-ecca-50de-8256-302276a8c0c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed6d0ded-ecca-50de-8256-302276a8c0c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448323} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d641374-fb2b-5515-9551-b1f94e91baca" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4626da49-16af-5f92-be8b-0ede6458b582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448324} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ac4ea5-c3ac-52b8-b780-d761ee6ccd2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4626da49-16af-5f92-be8b-0ede6458b582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448324} :answer-field/id #uuid "7af67d6f-4108-5880-b4ff-5f30c21746cc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48d9b691-f927-556a-a0f4-054f943d7dcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-129240" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x-y+2z=0$ and $9x-3y+6z+5=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- **II.** The planes are parallel but not coincident.\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x-y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,-1,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $9x-3y+6z+5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨9,-3,6⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${n}_{2}=3{n}_{1}.$ So, the normal vectors are parallel.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. \n\nFor the two planes to coincide, the equation of one plane should be a scalar multiple of the other. However, if we try to manipulate the equation of the second plane to resemble the equation of the first plane, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-3y+6z+5=0 \\\\ 3x-y+2z+\\frac{5}{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nClearly, this equation is not the same as the equation of the first plane. So, the planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3bf1a8d-9dfc-5a03-8a7a-a12552a416b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448326} {:answer/id #uuid "30b819cc-54c9-5241-bcb2-0afe25ea1cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3bf1a8d-9dfc-5a03-8a7a-a12552a416b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448326} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9949ae3-b6d9-5ef1-8624-bc499988813e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449203} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f26368b7-3e6e-5297-9b4f-7695649ea137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448328} {:answer/id #uuid "d00fa2fb-b244-56ee-b0ac-1b84182ea9ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f26368b7-3e6e-5297-9b4f-7695649ea137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448328} :answer-field/id #uuid "c385d683-72a4-5ea4-b2a1-efdb9c6df55d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449204} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8b6f951-e1c6-5513-a35c-3fa485d07fab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448330} {:answer/id #uuid "8c5c44e0-de54-563d-a94e-0a2b9889f8e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c5c44e0-de54-563d-a94e-0a2b9889f8e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448331} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c21207d-f238-50e0-bf4e-370792bcf5f4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c9f9477f-0f39-55d8-91e7-cff41b6de7c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-129241" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-3y+2z=0$ and $x-2y+5=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n\n- **II.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-3y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-3,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-2,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨4,2,1⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7823cc1d-e72d-50f4-af52-e5710e6619a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448332} {:answer/id #uuid "057d0176-e1f4-520c-a143-aa4e8964f2f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7823cc1d-e72d-50f4-af52-e5710e6619a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448332} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdffdf7c-e7ca-5a79-9cff-9ff74a794c8e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449206} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "555b8c2a-281e-59e0-989a-153d03514140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448334} {:answer/id #uuid "637cc037-e978-545a-891a-ad0bd8723150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555b8c2a-281e-59e0-989a-153d03514140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448334} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a72e661-92ba-514e-9b21-9c405c4b262e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030f35ea-269a-5b9f-b30e-0d3d46f40283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448336} {:answer/id #uuid "b29d3efe-e9d0-57f7-894c-28ab8000018d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b29d3efe-e9d0-57f7-894c-28ab8000018d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448337} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eee5865-067e-555f-8847-0162ac1e2d3e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d75bf5e3-9255-56f7-a884-2df425d0b593" :question/math-academy-id "q-129258" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-5y+2z=0$ and $3x-2y+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n\n- **II.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-5y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-5,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x-2y+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-5,2⟩\\times ⟨3,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+6j+13k \\\\  & =⟨4,6,13⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b0007c9-b9d9-5073-9847-1328f8ba456f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448338} {:answer/id #uuid "c07d5de8-6189-5107-a5d0-b648d30f4e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b0007c9-b9d9-5073-9847-1328f8ba456f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448338} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c49eabf-4bf6-5c32-9685-79efc670c417" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449209} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14bb3934-f6ec-59cd-99ae-ebf070b84930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448340} {:answer/id #uuid "a7dc5079-c112-5095-af24-842397e211d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7dc5079-c112-5095-af24-842397e211d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448341} :answer-field/id #uuid "55c3de56-e97c-5d08-8dd0-16889f5908a4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449210} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb8a1855-4689-53bf-ad30-730d170807be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448342} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4d1237-b5dc-5cb5-86d5-1b7a288207c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb8a1855-4689-53bf-ad30-730d170807be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448342} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dd284aa-2269-52c0-a105-e2d1597fba9e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df6925db-161f-5f40-8f9d-0f308e52b4c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-129259" :question/problem "Given the two planes $2x-y+3z=0$ and $5x-2y+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨7,15,2⟩.$\n- **II.** The planes intersect on a line.\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $2x-y+3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-1,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $5x-2y+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨5,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\times ⟨5,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =6i+15j+k \\\\  & =⟨6,15,1⟩\\ne ⟨7,15,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes cannot be coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "225965e7-ea8b-53cc-8c0e-59f84b35bad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448344} {:answer/id #uuid "44625f5b-937b-5938-b07c-f560e2643779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44625f5b-937b-5938-b07c-f560e2643779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448345} :answer-field/id #uuid "d07dfd5a-6ecb-5608-b7c1-bea7db6ba11f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f406006b-6b33-5be7-af63-0ad0b245352f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448346} {:answer/id #uuid "f15dcac9-93bd-55b2-9f31-b7ee83d2ce65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f406006b-6b33-5be7-af63-0ad0b245352f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448346} :answer-field/id #uuid "56b07353-6adf-5e95-9046-04d5131fb4b2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d244ee5-d55d-5d5d-a779-19cd20f8d3e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448348} {:answer/id #uuid "81250b54-fda0-5220-8698-e14b62c96958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81250b54-fda0-5220-8698-e14b62c96958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448349} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f1dcfe-3ed7-5654-8b55-b7e27497c7e8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "999cfdc7-ea79-5a7b-bd15-dce6f8b9e282" :question/math-academy-id "q-129260" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x+y-2z=0$ and $2x+y+3z+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨5,-13,1⟩.$\n- **II.** The planes are parallel.\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x+y-2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+y+3z+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,1,3⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,1,-2⟩\\times ⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =5i-13j+k \\\\  & =⟨5,-13,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the corresponding planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only I and III only are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9480da-b8d7-5635-acad-ba1da8240664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448350} {:answer/id #uuid "ac1933c0-bd2f-5aff-beae-cb8cda84293b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b9480da-b8d7-5635-acad-ba1da8240664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448350} :answer-field/id #uuid "f40e5e28-4f88-5130-b328-64606e612555" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449215} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b291afa3-882c-5323-96b3-be71495fa5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448352} {:answer/id #uuid "c25385b7-80d0-51da-88a9-662a5e5b2c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c25385b7-80d0-51da-88a9-662a5e5b2c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448353} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a4987ef-c77c-5b41-994f-27c06e153327" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449216} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a59e55b-0aa1-51df-b3d5-69f5f25a9700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448354} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf7ba73-0774-51da-bccc-e7f1bc26d6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a59e55b-0aa1-51df-b3d5-69f5f25a9700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448354} :answer-field/id #uuid "71c03d44-f207-5cb2-b332-ad7675261ad8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9644136-e70e-5412-95e4-ddf24de80c84" :question/math-academy-id "q-129261" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-y+2z=0$ and $5x+y-13=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨-3,12,6⟩.$\n- **II.** The planes intersect on a line.\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $5x+y-13=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨5,1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-1,2⟩\\times ⟨5,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2i+10j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,10,6⟩\\ne ⟨-3,12,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the corresponding planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes could not be coincident either.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29610715-333d-5e0c-9328-eec1d45f56ed" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Limits Along Different Paths for Multivariable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e982015-e57d-5a0b-a9cf-5d08deab7ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448356} {:answer/id #uuid "2459a454-5301-5e77-b21b-b6196bab14e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2459a454-5301-5e77-b21b-b6196bab14e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448357} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d95f94d-2076-5218-bb4b-c6ab553eb89a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449218} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b6df36c-4778-5e0d-8a29-4c2efc4da127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448358} {:answer/id #uuid "51ef316d-e1c9-5b72-9ff3-7956a1c2c951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b6df36c-4778-5e0d-8a29-4c2efc4da127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448358} :answer-field/id #uuid "b396f2c8-dc63-5102-8ab9-0b273481f509" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449219} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23411fdc-77e6-57da-b87b-f1f0a95f66cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448360} {:answer/id #uuid "ff37351c-4fe5-5bcc-ab1b-336319013805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff37351c-4fe5-5bcc-ab1b-336319013805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448361} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0e78afc-fd6f-5a29-a353-29016479df8c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449220}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88abe9a3-7bd6-5ff9-8f3e-e809f8b5b178" :question/math-academy-id "q-129406" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2xy}{3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=0$\n- **II.** The limit evaluates to $\\frac{2}{3}$ along the path $y=x$\n- **III.** The limit does not exist" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2xy}{3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{2(0)(0)}{3({0}^{2})-{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=0}\\,\\frac{2xy}{3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2x(0)}{3({0}^{2})-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{2xy}{3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x(x)}{3{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2xy}{3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29610715-333d-5e0c-9328-eec1d45f56ed" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Limits Along Different Paths for Multivariable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "810c6a8f-0958-52c6-b20f-d96a37359b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448362} {:answer/id #uuid "08cfa10d-b846-5e6d-bf35-9404324b2a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "810c6a8f-0958-52c6-b20f-d96a37359b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448362} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd5e3b0a-5393-557f-b53b-8a481a907ef0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449221} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88619661-430d-5de8-b84b-ec40f974019f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448364} {:answer/id #uuid "1a45e285-3045-5c04-8840-34af5a94d221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a45e285-3045-5c04-8840-34af5a94d221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448365} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cee3926-16f6-5e9e-9417-558226515e81" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449222} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e8e63f-6e04-57b4-8a7d-297ae9238284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448366} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec1f619-5c35-5d30-81b4-076f333cd284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ec1f619-5c35-5d30-81b4-076f333cd284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448367} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1158047-7645-528c-878f-9126eb72416b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7bd92abc-0899-50b8-83be-62e32b920d95" :question/math-academy-id "q-129408" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The limit evaluates to $4$ along the path $y={x}^{4}$\n- **II.** The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $x=0$\n- **III.** The limit does not exist" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{2({0}^{2})\\sqrt{0}}{{0}^{4}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{4}}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{4}}}{{x}^{4}+({x}^{4})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{8}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}(1+{x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2\\cancel{{x}^{4}}}{\\cancel{{x}^{4}}(1+{x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2}{1+{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+{0}^{4}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,x=0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{y\\to 0}\\frac{2({0}^{2})\\sqrt{y}}{{0}^{4}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{y\\to 0}0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb45ac63-db12-5103-a680-0aca60a50ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448368} {:answer/id #uuid "a12d2978-9d54-59d4-9961-6bdc86f3c49f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb45ac63-db12-5103-a680-0aca60a50ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448368} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0935ce5-8cb9-5439-9df5-d68f6b26b1b4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fb2ec2a-0f20-512b-93a8-4b9f3c962c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448370} {:answer/id #uuid "022054e0-5021-5992-9a69-680cffbd01c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fb2ec2a-0f20-512b-93a8-4b9f3c962c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448370} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2774138-c2fc-5876-84c5-93da8a175e9f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449225} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb2b2b09-edcc-581e-920d-e47a8346fc6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448372} {:answer/id #uuid "c8393209-b177-529e-b28b-4beba3d7980d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8393209-b177-529e-b28b-4beba3d7980d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448373} :answer-field/id #uuid "887210a3-979a-5046-a639-10af689a9ba1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449226}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22b7c2e7-9621-5013-a411-a722a7ceea01" :question/math-academy-id "q-129437" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $RS$ is well defined\n- **II.** The product $RP$ is well defined\n- **III.** The product $SP$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $P$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $R$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{5\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $S$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $S$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false."}]}
